<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khuc Hao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/917">917</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Khúc Hạo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khuc Hao was a Vietnamese governor of the Tinh Hai circuit, the former Tang <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> of Annam, from 907 to 917. Succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khuc-thua-du">Khuc Thua Du</a>, he ruled autonomously while professing loyalty to Chinese courts, reorganising local administration, taxes and labour service. His reforms are seen as an early step towards an independent Vietnamese state.</p></div>
